- (security/obs/design) A panic after init with a resolved instance leaves:
  - exactly one single-line `event:"panic"` home-level line with no payload;
  - one `detail-run.ndjson` line with `panic_payload` and a `backtrace` array that validates against
    `schemas/diag-detail.v1.json`;
  - nothing on stderr;
  - on Unix, 0600 files in 0700 dirs.

  The witness is `panic_hook_writes_detail_line_with_payload_and_backtrace` and `write_detail_…`. This is proven
  in-process; see Constraints (per security-plan §Bootstrap `logging-redaction-wire`; obs-plan §7 Panic hooks;
  design-system §Surface: cli "Stack traces").

- (arch/security/obs) The level comes only from `<home>/config.json` `diagnostics_level`:
  - absent file or key → INFO;
  - `"debug"` → DEBUG with an unchanged key set;
  - a bad value, a bad `v` or unknown keys → one `parse-rejected{parser:"config-json"}` line at WARN;
  - `RUST_LOG=trace` changes nothing.

  Witnessed by `read_diagnostics_level_*`, `run_config_*` and `run_rust_log_changes_nothing` (per architecture
  §Cross-cutting Patterns → Config management; security-plan §Anti-Patterns → Universal; obs-plan §11 Logs).

