  `tempfile::tempdir()` with a link made by the test:
  1. a plain base, absent then present, is created and kept as before (every OS);
  2. a link whose target is gone gets the target back, a directory with mode exactly 0700 (Unix);
  3. a link whose target is an owner-only directory is kept, an existing entry inside it untouched (Unix);
